# L §3.1/§3.3: a rate carries its period in its value; a bare 0 as a rate def's whole value states none, and the
# type `rate` gives none: LOAD-UNIT at load (L §8.4).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

def c: rate at reader
  rule base = 0

ask q: c law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
